### Comandas — Orders.API manual tests
### Run the requests top to bottom (VS Code "REST Client" extension, Visual Studio or Rider).
### Named requests (# @name) let later requests reuse ids from earlier responses.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5102

### 1. The menu (dishes and combos with calculated prices)
# @name menu
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/menu

### 2. Open an order for table 12
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableNumber": 12
}

### 3. Add 2 × the first menu item
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "menuItemId": "{{menu.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 4. Change that line to 3 units
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.lineId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 3
}

### 5. See the order (lines, subtotal, status)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### 6. Lifecycle: Created -> Confirmed -> InPreparation -> Ready -> Delivered
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/confirm

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/start-preparation

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/mark-ready

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/deliver

### 7. Final state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### 8. Invalid transition: cancelling a delivered order.
### Until step 2.11 (ProblemDetails) this returns a 500; afterwards a clear 4xx error.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
